 "requested_at": "2026-11-12T19:52:20.943270Z",
 "text": "The clause is **not enforceable**. The RTA does not allow a landlord to charge a late fee for rent. A $50 late charge is a prohibited charge, regardless of what the lease says. The landlord's remedy for late rent is the statutory process for nonpayment of rent, which runs through a notice of termination (Form N4) and an application to the Landlord and Tenant Board. It does not include a penalty charge.\n\nSection 133 is the provision that decides this. I'm citing it from memory, so please confirm the wording against the current consolidation of the Act on e-Laws before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 133",
